I liked most of Alex Werner's suggestions, but I have a problem with this one:

>-You should be able to pay shopkeepers of the appropriate type to identify
>your items for you. So you could chat with a antique weapons dealer and he
>would (for half what it would cost to sell to you) identify any weapons you
>were carrying

I have often used the following trick in games in whch this particular scheme is
implemented:
  Go to a shopkeeper.  Figure out how much things will cost.  Ask him to identify
an item for you.  Once he tells you how much it will cost, you know what it is,
roughly. 
  Perhaps it would be better to have a set price for ID'ing things, so that you
can't get away with such things.  Then, if you have a really powerful artifact or
whatever, you couln't figure it out because it would cost you 5000 zorkmids to ID
it.

